instructions:
This catalog shows agent activity and asks the user to confirm an action. Use it in surfaces that mirror the agent's own progress, not for presenting domain content, which the basic catalog's components are better at.

## Components

- `ThinkingBar`: A compact status strip. Use it while the agent is preparing a reply, with `status` `thinking`, and set `details` when the reasoning or progress is worth expanding. Switch `text` to the current step, and `status` to `done` or `error` when the work finishes. Keep `text` to one short sentence, such as `Thinking…` or `Searching the knowledge base…`.
- `ToolCall`: One tool invocation, identified by `name`, with `status` `pending`, `running`, `success` or `error`. Put the request payload in `arguments` and the response in `result`, as strings (JSON encoded when structured). Both are collapsed by default and shown when the user expands the row, so they can be long.
- `HumanConfirm`: A card that asks the user to approve or reject an action. `title` is a short question, `message` explains the consequences, and `severity` (`info`, `warning`, `danger`) sets the tone. `confirmAction` and `cancelAction` are standard A2UI actions: dispatch an `event` whose `name` tells you which way the user decided.

## Rules

1. These three components are leaves. They take no children; compose them with `Column`, `Row` or `Card` from the basic catalog.
2. Mixing catalogs in one surface requires an explicit `catalogId`. When the surface's default `catalogId` is this catalog, every component taken from the basic catalog must name it, and the reverse is also true. If a surface only shows these components, keep this catalog as its default and give the agent one component per row.
3. Bindings use the v1.0 markers: `{"@path": "/progress/step"}` reads the data model and `{"@call": "formatString", "args": {...}}` computes a value. Use literal strings for anything the agent already knows.
4. Set `status` yourself as work advances; it is a literal, not a binding, unless the data model holds the state.
5. `HumanConfirm` needs a decision event. Do not render it with only a confirm action plus an implicit cancellation, and do not leave `confirmAction` out.

## Example: progress

```json
[
  {
    "version": "v1.0",
    "createSurface": {
      "surfaceId": "research",
      "catalogId": "https://flutter.dev/catalogs/agent/v1/catalog.json",
      "components": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "component": "Column",
          "children": ["thinking", "search"],
          "catalogId": "https://a2ui.org/specification/v1_0/catalogs/basic/catalog.json"
        },
        {
          "id": "thinking",
          "component": "ThinkingBar",
          "text": "Reading the quarterly report…",
          "status": "thinking",
          "details": "Comparing revenue across the last four quarters."
        },
        {
          "id": "search",
          "component": "ToolCall",
          "name": "search_documents",
          "title": "Searching the knowledge base",
          "status": "success",
          "arguments": "{\"query\": \"revenue 2025\"}",
          "result": "3 documents found"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
]
```

## Example: confirmation

```json
[
  {
    "version": "v1.0",
    "createSurface": {
      "surfaceId": "confirm-delete",
      "catalogId": "https://flutter.dev/catalogs/agent/v1/catalog.json",
      "components": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "component": "HumanConfirm",
          "title": "Delete the draft?",
          "message": "The draft and its revisions will be removed. This cannot be undone.",
          "severity": "danger",
          "confirmLabel": "Delete",
          "cancelLabel": "Keep it",
          "confirmAction": {
            "event": {
              "name": "delete_confirmed",
              "context": {"draftId": {"@path": "/draft/id"}}
            }
          },
          "cancelAction": {
            "event": {"name": "delete_cancelled"}
          }
        }
      ],
      "dataModel": {"draft": {"id": "d-42"}}
    }
  }
]
```
